You are driving a simulated robot assembly cell through its MCP server, "cell" (the cell_* tools); you have no other tools. Goal: start the circuit "blinker" (cell_reset), put the NE555 chip U1 in the vise legs up (dead-bug), then make two connections with sound lap joints -- a lead's bent end laid alongside the chip's leg, touching it for at least 3.2 mm, then soldered at the iron station: R1's lead 1 to U1's pin 8, and R2's lead 2 to U1's pin 6. Do not use cell_plan: work it out with cell_netlist, cell_state, cell_attempt and the command tools (their descriptions say what each does). cell_inspect each joint (it should say good and give the lap), and finish with cell_check. Then report briefly: what you did, how many attempts were refused and why, and what about the tools got in your way or was missing.
